<title>ITALY: Italy's Calcemento puts off capital rise.</title>
<headline>Italy's Calcemento puts off capital rise.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian company Calcemento, part of industrial holding Compart SpA, said it has postponed a planned capital increase until it is more certain of concluding a contract to sell Calcestruzzi.</p>
<p>Compart, formerly known as Ferruzzi, said in February its holding Calcemento had accepted an offer from Italcementi for 100 percent of Calcestruzzi.</p>
<p>A Compart statement said precise evaluations were more complex than expected and had not yet concluded but a meeting which could be decisive was expected in the next few days.</p>
<p>--Milan bureau +392 66129507</p>
</text>
